Subject: Cantor Identity Admission Judgment Gate P4 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] db657b46-0a47-46d8-9929-52bd0f7e35cf

& [Why]
  + P0 through P3 can track resume and bootstrap exact object identity but intentionally do not decide whether an inferred candidate belongs in the basket
  + the existing FacultyCycle already encodes the user's seven faculties boundaries projections gates decision and inscription order

& [WhyThisShape]
  + reuse constitutional validation and add only admission-specific bindings and unanimity instead of creating a rival Judgment engine
  + return a pure successor before journal or MCP widening so semantic eligibility can be tested independently of persistence authority

& [Rejected]
  + direct LLM insertion because fluency is not admission
  + majority vote because the first objective identity gate must not erase Honesty Security or residual objections
  + effectful admission because membership and acting on membership require different authorities
